---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Real Ingredients · Purest Electrolyte"
  description="No sugar. No dyes. No ingredients you can't pronounce. Just freeze-dried real fruit and French gray sea salt. That's it."
>
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20 max-w-3xl">

    <a href="/about" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground mb-8 inline-block">← Back to About</a>

    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight mb-6">Real Ingredients. Nothing Else.</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      Turn over most electrolyte drinks and you'll find a paragraph of chemicals. Turn over Purest and you'll find two things: <strong>real freeze-dried fruit</strong> and <strong>French gray sea salt</strong>. That's the entire ingredient list.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-12">

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">What's Actually in Purest?</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="border-l-4 border-foreground pl-5 py-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-semibold text-lg mb-1">Freeze-Dried Real Fruit</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Whole fruit — ginger, limes, cherries, cranberries, hibiscus — freeze-dried to lock in flavor and natural sugars. No artificial flavoring. No concentrates. Real fruit.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-4 border-foreground pl-5 py-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-semibold text-lg mb-1">French Gray Sea Salt</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Hand-harvested from France's Atlantic coast. Unrefined, unbleached, naturally rich in 85+ trace minerals. Not the cheap table salt used in most sports drinks.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-4">What's NOT in Purest</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {[
            ["Added sugar", "No sucrose, fructose, or glucose added"],
            ["Artificial sweeteners", "No sucralose, aspartame, or synthetic sweeteners"],
            ["Food dyes", "No Red 40, Blue 1, Yellow 5 or any synthetic coloring"],
            ["Maltodextrin", "A cheap filler that spikes blood sugar — not here"],
            ["Natural flavors", "An industry loophole for lab-made chemicals — we use actual fruit"],
            ["Preservatives", "Nothing to extend shelf life artificially"],
            ["Anti-caking agents", "No silicon dioxide or other processing aids"],
          ].map(([title, desc]) => (
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start p-3 border-b border-border last:border-0">
              <div>
                <p class="text-sm font-medium">{title}</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-0.5">{desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">Why "Natural Flavors" Isn't Good Enough</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          You'll see "natural flavors" on almost every electrolyte drink label — including many marketed as "clean." Here's what that actually means: under FDA regulations, "natural flavors" can include hundreds of lab-derived chemical compounds as long as they originated from a natural source at some point in the process.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          At Purest, we don't use natural flavors. We use <em>actual freeze-dried fruit</em>. The flavor in your Ginger LimeAid isn't from a ginger-derived chemical compound — it's from real ginger that was freeze-dried whole. There's a difference, and you can taste it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">Why Freeze-Dried?</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Freeze-drying removes water from fruit at very low temperatures, preserving the natural flavor compounds, color, and nutrition that heat processing destroys. The result is fruit that tastes intensely like itself — and mixes into water to create a drink that actually tastes like fruit, not like a candy version of fruit.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          It's also how we keep the ingredient list so clean. Real freeze-dried fruit doesn't need additives to taste good or stay shelf-stable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">You Can See Through the Jar</h2>
        <p class="text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
          We use glass jars on purpose. You can look right through and see your electrolytes. There's nothing to hide. The powder looks like what it is — ground fruit and sea salt. If we were using artificial dyes or synthetic compounds, we wouldn't want you looking that closely.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-border">
      <a
        href="/products"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-foreground text-background px-8 py-3 text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity"
      >
        Shop Purest Electrolyte →
      </a>
    </div>

  </section>
</Layout>
